1
00:00:14,900 --> 00:00:17,717
These players who think it's
all about their agility,

2
00:00:17,800 --> 00:00:19,900
man, they're living in a dream.

3
00:00:20,480 --> 00:00:21,310
I mean, sure,

4
00:00:21,620 --> 00:00:23,617
firing speed and evasion are important,

5
00:00:23,700 --> 00:00:27,937
and time was, if you rock those two
things, it's all you needed to be the best.

6
00:00:28,020 --> 00:00:29,200
Till now, that is.

7
00:00:29,880 --> 00:00:33,217
Yeah, hate to say it, but it
don't work like that anymore.

8
00:00:33,300 --> 00:00:34,130
In fact,

9
00:00:34,213 --> 00:00:35,297
I got a message for
the folks who spent the

10
00:00:35,380 --> 00:00:38,027
last eight months indoors
boosting their AGI.

11
00:00:38,900 --> 00:00:41,020
Sucks to be you right now, Tony.

12
00:00:43,700 --> 00:00:47,997
Now that's the kind of comment we'd expect
from the top player of Gun Game Online,

13
00:00:48,080 --> 00:00:50,400
one of the most challenging VR Miss.

14
00:00:50,640 --> 00:00:52,111
Talk about controversial.

15
00:00:52,320 --> 00:00:55,257
I guess, but who knows if
I'll be on MMO stream again,

16
00:00:55,340 --> 00:00:56,897
so might as well stir things up.

17
00:00:56,980 --> 00:00:57,810
Oh, please.

18
00:00:57,893 --> 00:01:00,917
So, do you think you have a shot
in the upcoming bullet of bullets?

19
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:02,059
Damn right, honey.

20
00:01:02,240 --> 00:01:05,358
I wouldn't be in it if I
didn't think I could win it.

21
00:01:06,940 --> 00:01:09,020
It won't be that easy to succeed.

22
00:01:09,340 --> 00:01:12,458
The B .O .B.'s a solo journey,
so it's way different.

23
00:01:12,580 --> 00:01:15,697
What worked for you up to now
doesn't mean it'll work again.

24
00:01:15,780 --> 00:01:19,337
If I were you, I wouldn't chalk
my wins up to my status type.

25
00:01:19,420 --> 00:01:24,302
Yeah, well, if anything, my results point
to some big changes happening in G .G .O.

26
00:01:24,400 --> 00:01:26,437
You're all about A .G .I., Yamikaze.

27
00:01:26,520 --> 00:01:28,260
Go figure you'd be in denial.

28
00:01:29,700 --> 00:01:32,120
Wake up, people! Till now,

29
00:01:32,280 --> 00:01:34,397
the best strategy was
boosting your AGI and

30
00:01:34,480 --> 00:01:36,877
shooting a powerful gun
as fast as you could.

31
00:01:36,960 --> 00:01:41,217
But the reality is, the balance of
gameplay in an MMO is always changing.

32
00:01:41,300 --> 00:01:42,917
Especially in games like this one,

33
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:45,737
with levels that don't let
you respect your stats.

34
00:01:45,820 --> 00:01:49,137
You have to think ahead and be
smart when using your points,

35
00:01:49,220 --> 00:01:53,317
because the best weapon in one level
zone might not work for you in the next.

36
00:01:53,400 --> 00:01:54,237
Besides,

37
00:01:54,320 --> 00:01:56,237
the new guns coming out
are gonna have higher

38
00:01:56,320 --> 00:01:58,849
strength requirements
and accuracy bonuses.

39
00:02:01,380 --> 00:02:05,660
You remember when he was talking
about how great being an AGI type was?

40
00:02:05,800 --> 00:02:07,506
That dick totally scammed us.

41
00:02:13,580 --> 00:02:15,980
You're nothing but a fake sex seed.

42
00:02:16,320 --> 00:02:20,380
And now, you'll face judgement
from someone with real power.

43
00:02:35,640 --> 00:02:40,660
All I'm saying is, what's really important
in the end is the player's ability to...

44
00:02:51,300 --> 00:02:53,980
Uh-oh, I guess we have
a bad connection here.

45
00:02:54,220 --> 00:02:56,637
Don't worry, folks, I'm
sure he'll be back shortly.

46
00:02:56,720 --> 00:02:58,602
Stay tuned for more MMO's dream.

47
00:03:03,340 --> 00:03:06,177
This is real power, real strength.

48
00:03:06,260 --> 00:03:10,900
Let your fear carve one
name into your brains.

49
00:03:11,360 --> 00:03:14,700
The name I share with
this weapon, Death Gun.

50
00:03:32,840 --> 00:03:35,360
December 7th, 2025.

51
00:03:37,120 --> 00:03:38,800
Has it already been a year?

52
00:03:48,700 --> 00:03:53,160
I wonder what the difference is
between the real world and the virtual.

53
00:03:54,580 --> 00:03:56,840
The amount of data, that's all.

54
00:03:59,480 --> 00:04:00,820
You scared me.

55
00:04:01,260 --> 00:04:02,340
Sorry about that.

56
00:04:02,620 --> 00:04:03,796
I'm on time, though.

57
00:04:04,380 --> 00:04:05,210
What?

58
00:04:07,180 --> 00:04:08,420
No, I'm sorry.

59
00:04:08,660 --> 00:04:09,617
I was spacing out.

60
00:04:09,700 --> 00:04:10,957
Anyway, hello, Kirito.

61
00:04:11,040 --> 00:04:12,452
How are you doing today?

62
00:04:12,560 --> 00:04:15,700
It's been good so far,
but it's even better now.

63
00:04:16,800 --> 00:04:19,280
What are you staring at? Nothing.

64
00:04:19,600 --> 00:04:22,500
Just, uh, that outfit looks good on you.

65
00:04:22,940 --> 00:04:24,881
It brings back a lot of memories.

66
00:04:26,120 --> 00:04:27,220
I guess it does.

67
00:04:27,620 --> 00:04:28,837
No rapier, though.

68
00:04:28,920 --> 00:04:31,802
Looks like you went
overboard on the black today.

69
00:04:32,440 --> 00:04:33,270
Yeah.

70
00:04:33,353 --> 00:04:35,197
Sugu threw everything in
the wash this morning.

71
00:04:35,280 --> 00:04:36,880
And this is all I had left.

72
00:04:37,180 --> 00:04:39,239
Then stop putting your laundry off.

73
00:04:41,200 --> 00:04:44,494
I can't believe we both dressed
in our old colors today.

74
00:04:44,580 --> 00:04:46,109
What are the odds of that?

75
00:04:46,280 --> 00:04:49,377
Well, if we see each other
every day for a year, it's...

76
00:04:49,460 --> 00:04:51,777
That was a rhetorical
question, Smarty Pants.

77
00:04:51,860 --> 00:04:52,690
Come on.

78
00:04:52,773 --> 00:04:53,680
Okay, okay.

79
00:04:56,860 --> 00:05:01,036
I don't know about you, but I think
the Imperial Palace is interesting.

80
00:05:01,880 --> 00:05:02,710
Interesting?

81
00:05:02,793 --> 00:05:03,623
What do you mean?

82
00:05:04,360 --> 00:05:06,419
It's two kilometers north to south,

83
00:05:06,680 --> 00:05:10,540
1.5 east to west, and it
takes up 20 % of Chiyoda Ward.

84
00:05:10,820 --> 00:05:14,797
There aren't any subways or tunnels
under it, and it's a no-fly zone.

85
00:05:14,880 --> 00:05:16,577
It's kind of cool, don't you think?

86
00:05:16,660 --> 00:05:20,601
I mean, it's this big restricted
area right in the middle of Tokyo.

87
00:05:21,200 --> 00:05:25,906
Not only is it cut off from everything
physically, but information-wise as well.

88
00:05:26,100 --> 00:05:26,930
See that?

89
00:05:27,013 --> 00:05:28,368
It's a surveillance camera.

90
00:05:28,700 --> 00:05:31,657
This place was set up with
its very own closed network.

91
00:05:31,740 --> 00:05:34,211
You can't even access it from the outside.

92
00:05:34,840 --> 00:05:37,020
Wow, that's a weird-looking camera.

93
00:05:37,540 --> 00:05:38,370
Yeah.

94
00:05:38,480 --> 00:05:40,837
Not only is this place the heart of Tokyo,

95
00:05:40,920 --> 00:05:43,417
but it's also an isolated
world of its own.

96
00:05:43,500 --> 00:05:45,794
Maybe I'm exaggerating its cool factor.

97
00:05:45,880 --> 00:05:47,820
I get like that. You think?

98
00:05:54,260 --> 00:05:55,090
Wow.

99
00:05:56,020 --> 00:05:57,997
This used to be the inner citadel.

100
00:05:58,080 --> 00:05:59,140
Come on, let's go!

101
00:06:17,360 --> 00:06:20,377
Hey, you know that questionnaire
they gave us to fill out?

102
00:06:20,460 --> 00:06:22,217
The one about our future plans?

103
00:06:22,300 --> 00:06:24,418
Do you know what you want to do yet?

104
00:06:24,720 --> 00:06:25,550
Hmm.

105
00:06:25,633 --> 00:06:30,320
I guess, if anything, I want to go from
playing games to being a creator. A creator?

106
00:06:30,720 --> 00:06:31,760
What, for games?

107
00:06:32,140 --> 00:06:33,420
No, not for games.

108
00:06:33,660 --> 00:06:37,697
I want to make a human-machine interface
to replace the full-dive tech we use now.

109
00:06:37,780 --> 00:06:40,577
I've been going to all these tech
forums to learn more about it,

110
00:06:40,660 --> 00:06:43,601
but it's a heck of a lot
of information to absorb.

111
00:06:45,960 --> 00:06:49,277
After I graduate, all I
want is to be with you. Huh?

112
00:06:49,360 --> 00:06:53,960
I mean, I wish we could figure out a
way to live with Yui in this world, too.

113
00:06:54,600 --> 00:06:56,117
We'll be able to live with her someday,

114
00:06:56,200 --> 00:06:59,917
as soon as we figure out how to
access augmented reality at will.

115
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:03,417
The only thing standing in the way is
the difference in the amount of data.

116
00:07:03,500 --> 00:07:06,157
Didn't you say something
like that a little while ago?

117
00:07:06,240 --> 00:07:10,277
That the difference between our world
and the virtual was the amount of data?

118
00:07:10,360 --> 00:07:12,007
What does that mean, anyway?

119
00:07:12,340 --> 00:07:13,170
Let's see.

120
00:07:13,400 --> 00:07:14,282
It's like this.

121
00:07:14,440 --> 00:07:16,557
If we were holding hands in AOLO,

122
00:07:16,640 --> 00:07:19,875
it wouldn't be the same as
in the real world, would it?

123
00:07:20,580 --> 00:07:21,997
No, it wouldn't.

124
00:07:22,080 --> 00:07:24,980
You can feel a lot more
touching a real hand.

125
00:07:25,600 --> 00:07:28,617
Hey, is that what you mean by the
difference in the amount of data?

126
00:07:28,700 --> 00:07:29,530
Yep.

127
00:07:29,613 --> 00:07:31,257
And can you imagine
what it would be like if

128
00:07:31,340 --> 00:07:33,757
we could reproduce the
feel of skin in a pulse?

129
00:07:33,840 --> 00:07:37,937
Would we be able to tell the difference
between a real hand and an avatar's hand?

130
00:07:38,020 --> 00:07:41,080
I know I could, if I
was touching your hand.

131
00:07:42,480 --> 00:07:44,320
But it's not just touch, is it?

132
00:07:44,520 --> 00:07:45,537
I mean, in the real world,

133
00:07:45,620 --> 00:07:49,157
we get a lot of information from
how something sounds or tastes.

134
00:07:49,240 --> 00:07:52,297
Even if our atmosphere rigs
could access augmented reality,

135
00:07:52,380 --> 00:07:54,204
we'd still know the difference.

136
00:07:54,860 --> 00:07:58,817
Yeah, the second you saw or touched
something, you'd know if it was real or not.

137
00:07:58,900 --> 00:08:03,157
But hopefully, someone will come along
and make a technological breakthrough.

138
00:08:03,240 --> 00:08:07,880
And whatever that is, it'll have to
output a ton of sensory data all the time.

139
00:08:08,460 --> 00:08:12,857
Then we could break down the wall between
both worlds and be with Yui forever.

140
00:08:12,940 --> 00:08:15,177
Do you think that day
will ever come for us?

141
00:08:15,260 --> 00:08:16,090
Yeah.

142
00:08:16,173 --> 00:08:18,780
Then get to work and make
it happen, okay? Okay?

143
00:08:38,660 --> 00:08:40,020
Welcome, sir.

144
00:08:42,760 --> 00:08:44,440
Hey, Kirito!

145
00:08:44,680 --> 00:08:45,700
Over here!

146
00:08:53,420 --> 00:08:54,250
Go ahead.

147
00:08:54,500 --> 00:08:56,660
Order whatever you want. It's on me.

148
00:08:57,240 --> 00:08:58,122
Thank you, sir.

149
00:08:58,280 --> 00:09:00,420
That's very kind of you. Come on.

150
00:09:00,560 --> 00:09:02,257
You don't have to be so formal with me.

151
00:09:02,340 --> 00:09:04,869
Relax and talk to me
like you would in ALO.

152
00:09:05,480 --> 00:09:06,310
Okay.

153
00:09:06,393 --> 00:09:09,820
If you say so, then I guess I'll...

154
00:09:15,440 --> 00:09:21,600
I'd like the parfait au chocolate, the
framboise milfouille, and a hazelnut latte.

155
00:09:23,720 --> 00:09:26,177
Sorry to make you come all
the way out here, Kirito.

156
00:09:26,260 --> 00:09:29,597
If you're that sorry about it,
why'd you ask me to come to Ginza?

157
00:09:29,680 --> 00:09:33,386
Oh, and do you think you cannot
call me by that name in public?

158
00:09:33,820 --> 00:09:35,437
What's with all the attitude?

159
00:09:35,520 --> 00:09:36,873
I thought we were buds.

160
00:09:37,520 --> 00:09:40,755
I was the first to visit you
in the hospital, remember?

161
00:09:42,860 --> 00:09:43,690
He's right.

162
00:09:44,140 --> 00:09:47,258
When I came to, the first
one there wasn't my family.

163
00:09:47,380 --> 00:09:49,498
It was the leader of the task force.

164
00:09:50,760 --> 00:09:51,701
Seijiro Kikuoka,

165
00:09:51,820 --> 00:09:56,037
from the Tech Bureau at the Ministry
of Internal Affairs and Communications,

166
00:09:56,120 --> 00:09:56,950
a .k .a.

167
00:09:57,033 --> 00:09:58,387
the Virtual Reality Section.

168
00:10:03,360 --> 00:10:04,897
So what'd you want to see me about?

169
00:10:04,980 --> 00:10:08,760
If it's anything SAO-related,
I told you everything I know.

170
00:10:09,960 --> 00:10:13,078
Actually, I want to talk to
you about something else.

171
00:10:14,180 --> 00:10:15,356
Have a look at that.

172
00:10:17,040 --> 00:10:17,870
Who's he?

173
00:10:18,560 --> 00:10:19,960
This won't be pleasant.

174
00:10:20,620 --> 00:10:23,160
So last month, on November the 14th,

175
00:10:23,300 --> 00:10:26,065
the landlord of an
apartment complex in Nakano,

176
00:10:26,180 --> 00:10:28,197
Tokyo, noticed a foul odor while cleaning.

177
00:10:28,280 --> 00:10:30,137
It was coming from one of the units.

178
00:10:30,220 --> 00:10:33,396
So he disabled the lock and
discovered this man, dead.

179
00:10:33,720 --> 00:10:36,426
His name was Tamotsu
Shigemura when he was 26.

180
00:10:36,740 --> 00:10:38,446
He'd been dead for five days.

181
00:10:38,900 --> 00:10:40,194
They found him in bed.

182
00:10:40,380 --> 00:10:42,417
His place was a mess,
but no signs of burglary.

183
00:10:42,500 --> 00:10:45,382
He had something interesting
on his head, though.

184
00:10:45,920 --> 00:10:47,720
An amrusphere? Yeah.

185
00:10:48,480 --> 00:10:51,677
It was ruled an unnatural
death, so they did an autopsy.

186
00:10:51,760 --> 00:10:54,917
The cause of death was found
to be acute heart failure.

187
00:10:55,000 --> 00:10:56,360
Wait, heart failure?

188
00:10:56,640 --> 00:10:58,228
You mean his heart stopped?

189
00:10:58,480 --> 00:10:59,740
They find out why?

190
00:11:00,100 --> 00:11:01,180
No, they didn't.

191
00:11:03,060 --> 00:11:04,119
Here you are, sir.

192
00:11:07,960 --> 00:11:08,790
Unfortunately,

193
00:11:08,873 --> 00:11:10,717
since so much time had
passed since his death

194
00:11:10,800 --> 00:11:12,997
and foul play was ruled out as the cause,

195
00:11:13,080 --> 00:11:14,837
the autopsy wasn't very thorough.

196
00:11:14,920 --> 00:11:16,997
We do know he'd been
logged in for two days

197
00:11:17,080 --> 00:11:20,021
straight and hadn't eaten
anything the whole time.

198
00:11:20,400 --> 00:11:22,157
Well, that's not that unusual.

199
00:11:22,240 --> 00:11:23,828
Players do it all the time.

200
00:11:24,080 --> 00:11:25,917
Wait, why are you telling me about this?

201
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:29,157
He had a game installed on his
system called Gun Gale Online.

202
00:11:29,240 --> 00:11:30,157
You know that one?

203
00:11:30,240 --> 00:11:31,500
Yeah, GGO.

204
00:11:31,820 --> 00:11:34,938
It's the only MMO in Japan
with professional players.

205
00:11:35,460 --> 00:11:40,137
This past October, there was a tournament
to decide the most powerful player in GGO.

206
00:11:40,220 --> 00:11:42,338
The deceased was the guy who won it.

207
00:11:42,680 --> 00:11:44,621
His character's name was Zekseed.

208
00:11:45,320 --> 00:11:48,500
Was he playing GGO when he died? No.

209
00:11:48,720 --> 00:11:53,760
When it happened, he was appearing on a
show called MMO Stream as Zekseed's avatar.

210
00:11:54,340 --> 00:11:56,164
We know the time from the logs.

211
00:11:57,020 --> 00:11:59,961
This next bit of info still
needs to be confirmed.

212
00:12:00,400 --> 00:12:02,317
According to another player's blog,

213
00:12:02,400 --> 00:12:07,282
at the same time Shigemura had the heart
attack, something strange happened in GGO.

214
00:12:07,500 --> 00:12:08,330
What?

215
00:12:08,413 --> 00:12:10,957
Some players were at a bar
in-game watching the show when

216
00:12:11,040 --> 00:12:14,237
one of the players stood up
and started acting erratically.

217
00:12:14,320 --> 00:12:15,580
The blog states,

218
00:12:15,800 --> 00:12:18,337
The player was shouting stuff
about judgment and power

219
00:12:18,420 --> 00:12:21,773
at Zexeed's image on the TV
and then fired his gun at it.

220
00:12:22,340 --> 00:12:26,057
At the time, another player in the
bar happened to be recording audio.

221
00:12:26,140 --> 00:12:27,964
He uploaded it to a video site.

222
00:12:28,720 --> 00:12:32,220
Since the file had a Japan
Standard Time counter embedded.

223
00:12:33,020 --> 00:12:35,097
We know that the shot fired at the TV and

224
00:12:35,180 --> 00:12:37,317
Shigemura's avatar
disappearing from the show?

225
00:12:37,400 --> 00:12:39,282
happened at about the same time.

226
00:12:39,880 --> 00:12:41,409
Probably just coincidence.

227
00:12:41,800 --> 00:12:44,520
There was another death, though. What?

228
00:12:44,880 --> 00:12:49,820
This one happened on November the
28th, somewhere in Saitama Prefecture.

229
00:12:50,220 --> 00:12:51,500
Same setup as before.

230
00:12:51,780 --> 00:12:53,757
The deceased was found in their apartment.

231
00:12:53,840 --> 00:12:56,377
A guy delivering the newspaper
happened to look in the window.

232
00:12:56,460 --> 00:12:59,754
He saw the victim lying in
bed wearing an AmuSphere rig.

233
00:12:59,880 --> 00:13:01,115
Said the smell was...

234
00:13:03,340 --> 00:13:06,077
Let's skip the details of
the corpse's condition.

235
00:13:06,160 --> 00:13:08,807
Anyway, heart failure
was the cause of death.

236
00:13:09,020 --> 00:13:11,760
The victim was also a
top-ranking GGO player.

237
00:13:12,020 --> 00:13:15,020
His character's name was Usushio Tarako?

238
00:13:15,280 --> 00:13:17,217
Well, he was playing when he died.

239
00:13:17,300 --> 00:13:19,888
It happened in the
central plaza in Glocken.

240
00:13:20,040 --> 00:13:22,922
He was in the middle of
a meeting with his squad.

241
00:13:23,340 --> 00:13:25,399
I guess that's the same as a guild.

242
00:13:26,460 --> 00:13:29,872
A strange player went up to
him and shot him, point-blank.

243
00:13:30,020 --> 00:13:33,200
Do you know if it was the
same guy who shot Zekseed?

244
00:13:33,500 --> 00:13:34,380
Most likely.

245
00:13:34,760 --> 00:13:36,977
He said stuff about judgment and power,

246
00:13:37,060 --> 00:13:39,957
and then identified himself
with the same character name.

247
00:13:40,040 --> 00:13:40,870
What name?

248
00:13:42,360 --> 00:13:43,240
Death Gun.

249
00:13:44,280 --> 00:13:45,400
Death Gun?

250
00:13:52,480 --> 00:13:56,100
Are you absolutely sure both
victims died from heart failure?

251
00:13:56,460 --> 00:13:57,460
What do you mean?

252
00:13:58,420 --> 00:14:00,596
Was there any damage to their brains?

253
00:14:01,920 --> 00:14:03,802
I was wondering about that, too.

254
00:14:04,120 --> 00:14:08,077
So I asked the coroner if he found any
trace of damage to either of their brains,

255
00:14:08,160 --> 00:14:10,042
and he said they were both fine.

256
00:14:11,100 --> 00:14:14,057
Besides, the NerveGear rig
used high-output microwaves,

257
00:14:14,140 --> 00:14:17,257
powerful enough to fry the signal
elements and destroy the brain.

258
00:14:17,340 --> 00:14:18,337
On the other hand,

259
00:14:18,420 --> 00:14:20,137
the Amusphere rig was designed so that it

260
00:14:20,220 --> 00:14:22,817
couldn't emit electromagnetic
waves that powerful.

261
00:14:22,900 --> 00:14:25,429
At least, that's what
the developers claim.

262
00:14:25,520 --> 00:14:28,197
It sounds like you guys
have done your homework,

263
00:14:28,280 --> 00:14:32,440
but even so, your story's built
around coincidence and rumors. True.

264
00:14:32,680 --> 00:14:34,877
It could be a coincidence or even a hoax.

265
00:14:34,960 --> 00:14:36,077
I'm not sold either way.

266
00:14:36,160 --> 00:14:38,780
For now, and this is
hypothetical, mind you.

267
00:14:39,060 --> 00:14:42,597
Do you think it's even remotely
possible to stop a player's

268
00:14:42,680 --> 00:14:46,445
heart in the real world with
virtual bullets from a virtual gun?

269
00:15:04,960 --> 00:15:06,600
No, I don't think so.

270
00:15:06,920 --> 00:15:08,360
But hypothetically,

271
00:15:08,780 --> 00:15:11,497
let's say this death gun
did send some kind of killer

272
00:15:11,580 --> 00:15:14,517
signal to Zekseed and that
Tarako guy's ammospheres.

273
00:15:14,600 --> 00:15:15,600
What would it be?

274
00:15:16,020 --> 00:15:18,720
Could the sensation of
a touch stop a heart?

275
00:15:18,940 --> 00:15:20,780
Maybe a taste or smell?

276
00:15:21,200 --> 00:15:22,720
A sight, a sound?

277
00:15:22,860 --> 00:15:24,460
Or some other sensation?

278
00:15:27,400 --> 00:15:28,400
Okay, whoa.

279
00:15:28,780 --> 00:15:30,997
You already thought of this, haven't you?

280
00:15:31,080 --> 00:15:32,340
Oh, I get it.

281
00:15:32,500 --> 00:15:37,077
You and your team can't figure it out, so
you invite me for coffee to pick my brain?

282
00:15:37,160 --> 00:15:38,677
No, what are you talking about?

283
00:15:38,760 --> 00:15:41,037
I'd never do something
like that to you, honest.

284
00:15:41,120 --> 00:15:43,897
I liked talking to you and
just wanted your opinion.

285
00:15:43,980 --> 00:15:44,810
We're done.

286
00:15:45,200 --> 00:15:46,317
You want my opinion?

287
00:15:46,400 --> 00:15:47,230
Here it is.

288
00:15:47,313 --> 00:15:50,757
You can't stop a player's heart in
the real world by actions in-game.

289
00:15:50,840 --> 00:15:53,137
Shots fired and the heart
attacks are coincidences.

290
00:15:53,220 --> 00:15:54,050
Wait, hold on.

291
00:15:54,133 --> 00:15:55,476
Listen, you can order something else.

292
00:15:55,740 --> 00:15:57,916
Just sit down and hang out for a bit.

293
00:15:59,280 --> 00:16:00,110
Please.

294
00:16:00,193 --> 00:16:02,877
I can't tell you how relieved I
am to hear you put it into words.

295
00:16:02,960 --> 00:16:05,313
Fact is, I'm of the same opinion as you.

296
00:16:05,480 --> 00:16:09,715
I don't believe these two deaths were
caused by in-game gunshots either.

297
00:16:09,980 --> 00:16:12,857
And now that we've talked, I
want to ask you officially.

298
00:16:12,940 --> 00:16:15,537
Would you log into Gun
Gale Online and make

299
00:16:15,620 --> 00:16:18,561
contact with the player
calling himself Death Gun?

300
00:16:19,120 --> 00:16:21,355
And once I do find the guy, then what?

301
00:16:21,940 --> 00:16:23,757
You want me to get shot, is that it?

302
00:16:23,840 --> 00:16:25,000
Whoa now, come on.

303
00:16:25,140 --> 00:16:25,970
Well, screw that.

304
00:16:26,053 --> 00:16:27,468
I don't want to get killed.

305
00:16:28,260 --> 00:16:29,436
That's not possible.

306
00:16:29,640 --> 00:16:31,758
We just agreed it wasn't, didn't we?

307
00:16:32,240 --> 00:16:35,517
Besides, this Death Gun guy is
only going after specific targets.

308
00:16:35,600 --> 00:16:37,397
They have to meet his criteria.

309
00:16:37,480 --> 00:16:38,540
Criteria? Uh-huh.

310
00:16:40,060 --> 00:16:41,001
Here's the deal.

311
00:16:41,540 --> 00:16:44,357
Zekseed and Usushio Tarako
weren't just any old players.

312
00:16:44,440 --> 00:16:48,911
They were top-ranked, so it's safe to
assume he's not interested in newbies.

313
00:16:49,260 --> 00:16:51,717
But if you were strong enough to
beat Kayaba at his own game, then...

314
00:16:51,800 --> 00:16:52,630
That's different!

315
00:16:52,713 --> 00:16:55,797
Look, I don't know what you've
heard, but GGO's no walk in the park.

316
00:16:55,880 --> 00:16:57,237
It's filled with pro gamers!

317
00:16:57,320 --> 00:16:58,150
Hold the phone!

318
00:16:58,233 --> 00:16:59,217
You said pro gamer.

319
00:16:59,300 --> 00:17:00,737
What does that mean, pro?

320
00:17:00,820 --> 00:17:03,140
It means professional. Literally.

321
00:17:03,820 --> 00:17:06,697
Gungale Online is the only
virtual MMO with a game

322
00:17:06,780 --> 00:17:09,662
Control currency
conversion system in place.

323
00:17:09,880 --> 00:17:10,710
What?

324
00:17:10,793 --> 00:17:14,177
It means whatever money you earn in
the game gets paid back to you in cold,

325
00:17:14,260 --> 00:17:15,907
hard cash in the real world.

326
00:17:16,160 --> 00:17:18,217
Being a pro means you
have a constant stream

327
00:17:18,300 --> 00:17:20,597
of income from the game
coming in every month.

328
00:17:20,680 --> 00:17:25,504
And if you're a top player, that means
monthly you're making $200,000 to $300,000.

329
00:17:26,000 --> 00:17:27,176
It's an awesome gig.

330
00:17:27,520 --> 00:17:30,696
That's why the high-level
guys in GGO are so hardcore.

331
00:17:30,860 --> 00:17:34,919
They pour more time and passion into
it than players from other Miss.

332
00:17:35,380 --> 00:17:38,517
Someone like me can't just log
in and match players like that.

333
00:17:38,600 --> 00:17:39,837
You should find someone else.

334
00:17:39,920 --> 00:17:40,837
Whoa, hold it, hold it.

335
00:17:40,920 --> 00:17:42,017
Who else am I going to find?

336
00:17:42,100 --> 00:17:42,930
You're it.

337
00:17:43,013 --> 00:17:44,397
I need your help in this investigation.

338
00:17:44,480 --> 00:17:49,421
and if taking these pros on is going to be
that big a deal, I can pay you this much.

339
00:17:51,380 --> 00:17:53,637
I don't get why you're so hung up on this.

340
00:17:53,720 --> 00:17:56,955
You find horror stories like
these all the time online.

341
00:17:57,380 --> 00:17:58,400
Yeah, I know.

342
00:17:58,720 --> 00:18:00,955
But still, it's got my bosses worried.

343
00:18:01,160 --> 00:18:05,837
The effect of full-dive technology on the
real world is the hottest topic today.

344
00:18:05,920 --> 00:18:08,038
Literally everyone's researching it.

345
00:18:08,140 --> 00:18:11,657
People are going to try to use these
deaths to regulate the technology.

346
00:18:11,740 --> 00:18:14,397
We want to know the facts
before that happens.

347
00:18:14,480 --> 00:18:15,640
We want to be sure.

348
00:18:16,640 --> 00:18:18,237
That's why we're interested.

349
00:18:18,320 --> 00:18:22,180
You guys could just go directly
to the admins about it. Right.

350
00:18:22,500 --> 00:18:26,559
But Zaskar, the company that developed
and hosts GGO, is in the U .S.

351
00:18:26,960 --> 00:18:29,057
Their address, phone number, and email?

352
00:18:29,140 --> 00:18:32,434
None of it's been made public,
so we can't contact them.

353
00:18:32,900 --> 00:18:38,200
Ever since the seed was released, all kinds
of shady VR worlds have popped up. Yeah.

354
00:18:39,080 --> 00:18:41,117
Maybe they're legit, maybe they're not.

355
00:18:41,200 --> 00:18:43,057
But if we want to find anything out,

356
00:18:43,140 --> 00:18:46,277
the only way to do it is to try
contacting them in the game.

357
00:18:46,360 --> 00:18:48,184
I'm not asking you to get shot.

358
00:18:48,300 --> 00:18:51,037
We'll take whatever safety
precautions we have to.

359
00:18:51,120 --> 00:18:53,800
Just evaluate the
situation and report back.

360
00:18:54,180 --> 00:18:55,827
So will you help us or what?

361
00:18:59,760 --> 00:19:02,840
4,000 people died in Aincrad.

362
00:19:03,680 --> 00:19:08,060
It's been a year and finally those
memories are starting to fade.

363
00:19:08,820 --> 00:19:13,200
But now, more people are dying
in another virtual world,

364
00:19:13,400 --> 00:19:15,460
and I'm getting pulled back in.

365
00:19:16,240 --> 00:19:19,122
It's like someone doesn't
want me to ever forget.

366
00:19:24,380 --> 00:19:26,380
Oh, now I get it.

367
00:19:27,080 --> 00:19:30,057
I think I figured out why
you brought me here today.

368
00:19:30,140 --> 00:19:32,460
Oh, you did, huh? Mm-hmm.

369
00:19:33,280 --> 00:19:37,620
If our world is made up of an axis
called time and a plane called space,

370
00:19:37,900 --> 00:19:41,900
then the center of our reality is
this place, in the heart of Tokyo,

371
00:19:42,180 --> 00:19:43,886
where a castle used to stand.

372
00:19:44,580 --> 00:19:47,417
And the axis of all the
virtual worlds popping up now,

373
00:19:47,500 --> 00:19:51,500
thanks to the Seed, is a place that
also had a castle once, Aincrad.

374
00:19:52,120 --> 00:19:54,900
That's why this sunset
feels so nostalgic now.

375
00:19:57,280 --> 00:19:58,140
You're right.

376
00:19:58,560 --> 00:19:59,460
It does.

377
00:20:00,120 --> 00:20:03,417
You know, what you just said helped
me figure something out, too.

378
00:20:03,500 --> 00:20:04,330
Huh? Really?

379
00:20:04,900 --> 00:20:07,700
You remember what Aincrad
looked like? Well,

380
00:20:07,900 --> 00:20:12,697
maybe its shape was supposed to represent
the axis of time and the plane of space.

381
00:20:12,780 --> 00:20:13,610
Maybe.

382
00:20:13,693 --> 00:20:17,444
But if its vertical axis represented
time and its floor is space,

383
00:20:17,740 --> 00:20:20,337
then the Commander made a
world that tapered to nothing.

384
00:20:20,420 --> 00:20:22,891
Everything ended once you reached the top.

385
00:20:23,020 --> 00:20:26,117
Unfortunately, a certain
someone destroyed it halfway up.

386
00:20:26,200 --> 00:20:28,200
Now we'll never know how it ended.

387
00:20:28,400 --> 00:20:29,230
Yes, ma 'am.

388
00:20:29,460 --> 00:20:30,931
Sorry about that, ma 'am.

389
00:20:38,180 --> 00:20:40,180
Asuna, listen, I... What?

390
00:20:42,600 --> 00:20:43,430
Nah.

391
00:20:43,520 --> 00:20:44,717
Hey, it's getting cold.

392
00:20:44,800 --> 00:20:46,137
You want to start heading back now?

393
00:20:46,220 --> 00:20:47,050
Mm-hmm.

394
00:20:47,133 --> 00:20:49,817
Oh, and next time we come, let's
bring Liz and Leafa and the others.

395
00:20:49,900 --> 00:20:52,797
Wouldn't it be fun to get everyone
together for a picnic here?

396
00:20:52,880 --> 00:20:53,762
Yeah, it would.

397
00:20:54,060 --> 00:20:55,531
Especially in springtime.

398
00:21:10,540 --> 00:21:12,200
I'm in position. Roger.

399
00:21:12,680 --> 00:21:15,739
Targets haven't changed
their course or their speed.

400
00:21:15,920 --> 00:21:19,120
They're 400 meters from you, 1500 from me.

401
00:21:19,640 --> 00:21:20,470
Pretty far.

402
00:21:20,800 --> 00:21:22,094
Can you make the shot?

403
00:21:22,260 --> 00:21:25,160
No sweat. Okay, then. Fire when ready.

404
00:21:25,820 --> 00:21:27,357
I'm counting on you, Sinon.

405
00:21:27,440 --> 00:21:28,270
Roger.

406
00:21:32,420 --> 00:21:37,297
this pressure this anxiety this fear

407
00:21:37,380 --> 00:21:42,537
1500 meters that's nothing like tossing a

408
00:21:42,620 --> 00:21:46,617
lot of paper into a trash can no way

409
00:21:46,700 --> 00:21:50,320
this is nothing like how it felt that day

410
00:22:02,220 --> 00:22:03,620
Next

411
00:22:28,760 --> 00:22:31,560
Let's go.

412
00:22:56,160 --> 00:22:57,477
I'll

413
00:22:57,560 --> 00:22:58,877
see

414
00:22:58,960 --> 00:23:05,960
you

415
00:23:14,520 --> 00:23:16,300
next time.
